# corMani — build and runtime artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Local state: the mail store, the database, tokens, logs.
# NONE of this belongs in the repository — it is correspondence, and the
# database is rebuildable from the accounts themselves.
#
# `data/*` and not `data/`, and the difference is not cosmetic. `data/` ignores
# the DIRECTORY, and git will not un-ignore a file inside an ignored directory
# however many negations follow — so the three packaging assets below were
# silently excluded from every commit since stage 0. They existed on this
# machine, the test asserting their presence passed, and a fresh clone had
# none of them: no icon, no launcher, nothing for a Debian package to install.
# Ignoring the CONTENTS instead is what makes the exceptions possible.
data/*
!data/cormani.svg
!data/cormani.desktop
!data/*.metainfo.xml
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-*
*.mbox
*.eml
secrets.toml
google.txt
test.md
cormani.local.toml
tokens/
logs/

# Local working documents — author's machine, not the published tree.
# PLAN and SESSION_STATE are handoff notes; docs/accounts.txt holds real
# addresses; docs/imap.txt and toolkit-verification.txt are engineering notes.
PLAN.txt
SESSION_STATE.txt
CONVENTIONS.txt
docs/accounts.txt
docs/imap.txt
docs/toolkit-verification.txt
PUBLIC-RELEASE-AUDIT.txt
enhance.txt
ui.md
deb-plan.md
